            "accordion_row_7Qx4MJ": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What do Blue Light lenses do?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_MkpWgM": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Blue light glasses filter the blue light emissions from digital devices, artificial light from screens and lights and are used to minimise the impact on your circadian rhythm, which is particularly important for those who spend a lot of time using digital screens or in LED lit rooms. Blue light lenses can help mitigate the impact of blue light by limiting how much reaches the eyes, supporting the natural release of melatonin. Blue light lenses may contribute to improved hormone regulation and alertness.</p><p></p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
